          "id": "chapter-four-teenplaying-the-game-page-183",
          "level": 2,
          "title": "Page 183",
          "body": "Insufficient: “I just want different powers” · “Those powers didn’t\nTIER ACCESS THROUGH PLAY work out” · Retroactive changes that contradict established\nfiction.\nTIER ACCESS STARTING\nCAMPAIGN RANK UNLOCKED LEVEL\nStreet Level Tier 2 Level 5\nMid-Level Tier 3 Level 5\nPower Die size remains tied to Campaign\nRank regardless of which Tier is accessed. A\nStreet Level hero who accesses Tier 2 powers\nat Level 5 still uses d8 Power Dice.\nRESPEC\nAt Levels 3, 6, and 9, a hero may choose to Respec — an optional\ndecision made at the same time as the level-up. The player\nannounces their intention, establishes the story justification, and\npresents their rebuilt sheet at the start of the following session.\nWHAT A RESPEC CAN CHANGE\nOrigin, Class, and Ability Scores do not change through a\nRespec. These are identity. Everything else is eligible:\n▪ Powers — any Power Pick purchases, including Core Track\nsteps, Branch Powers, Utility Powers, and Enhancements.\nPower Sets themselves may be dropped or added within\nCampaign Rank limits.\n▪ Limitations — may be added, removed, or swapped, subject to\nCampaign Rank caps.\n▪ Skills and Specialties — any Skill training or Specialties\ngained at character creation or through advancement picks.\n▪ Talents — any Talent gained at Level 1 (if applicable), Level 3,\nor Level 9.\n▪ Merits and Flaws — any chosen at creation or gained through\nprior advancement. Origin-granted Merits and Flaws are part\nof the Origin package and cannot be changed through a\nRespec.\n▪ Calling — a hero whose motivational drive has genuinely\nshifted may change their Calling.\nTHE STORY REQUIREMENT\nA Respec does not happen between sessions as a paperwork\nexercise. It happens because something occurred in the fiction\nthat makes the change make sense. The GM confirms the\njustification is sufficient before the Respec takes effect. The bar\nis not high.\nSufficient vs. Insufficient Justification\nSufficient: A period of intensive training with a new mentor · A\ntraumatic encounter that changed how the hero’s powers\nmanifest · A philosophical shift or Calling change · A near-death\nexperience that forced a complete rebuild · Discovery that an\nearly assumption about their powers was wrong"
